6C(231)	KPJ	1987-01-31 10:16:38	Module MATCH had pointers from the low
					segment to the high segment (will this
					never end?). Initialize the pointers
					when we change segments.
		Changed: SEGRET@MONITO,MATBAK@MATCH

6C(230)	KPJ	1987-01-31 08:31:52	GETYNA did expect the "buffer" (in low
		segment) to contain a "string pointer" (to high segment).
		This does not work very well if we change high segments, since
		the strings move around, but the pointers still point at the
		old place.  Get rid of "string pointer" in the buffers in the
		low segment and use a table in the high segment to translate
		from file number to "string pointer" (pointer to ASCIZ).
		Change definitions of BUFFER macro to get rod of the pointers.
					<T10 only>
		Changed: (GETYNA,NAMTYP)@OBJSTA,KOMMAC

