KPJ	1985-06-14 14:59:12	Version 6B(10)-3:
		(a)	KOM-10 crashed when SET PHYSICAL LIMIT nnnP was used
			by the user. This was since SEE ignored the error
			returns from PAGE. ("cannot happen").
		(b)	UCD reported KOM-20 problem after editing. Same problem
			in KOM-10 if TMPCOR buffer allocation fails during
			EDIT commands.
		(c)	Bug in ERROR macro truncated the error message. New
			format of error report (including KOM-20 JSYS messages)
		(d)	Bug i PAGIN routine clobbered AC GP2.
		(e)	TMP:LME created and written only if a program-to-run
			has been set (.STPGM)
		(f)	"permanently" deleted from the WITHDRAW command,
			various versions.

	Changed: KOMMAC,COMPAR@COMPUT,(GTSOAR,SORACT,LISTPE,LISTAD)@LISPER,
